This derivative
--------------

  Dash Essential
  Copyright 2026 afrizal1221
  Licence: Apache License, Version 2.0

  Ported to the MediaTek MT6991 platform, device codename `dash`
  (POCO X8 Pro Max / REDMI Turbo 5 Max), based on upstream release v1.18.5.

  Modifications made in 2026 by afrizal1221:

  * Hardware handling rebuilt against the shipped `dash` kernel, device tree
    and ROM dump rather than carried over from MT6899: CPU and GPU frequency
    tables, thermal zones and cooling devices, MediaTek GED boost/ceiling
    OPP indices, UFS and DVFSRC memory nodes, touch and display interfaces,
    and the display resolution and density baseline.

  * Package renamed from io.github.neeschal.rodinessential to
    io.github.neeschal.dashessential; root module id renamed from
    nees_rodin_essential_backend to nees_dash_essential_backend; SELinux
    type, class and helper names moved into the `dash_*` namespace; binary
    and user-facing application and module strings renamed.

  * The deliverable of this derivative is the KernelSU Next / Magisk root
    module only. The upstream AOSP ROM integration is not built, tested or
    supported by this derivative.

  * The upstream release signing key is not held by this derivative, so
    module builds are signed with a local development key and carry a `-dev`
    suffix in the archive name.

  * Undocumented MT6899 fallback values were removed where a `dash` value
    could not be read at runtime: the daemon skips the control write rather
    than guessing at a value.

  * The upstream Flutter embedder engine release (v1.18.5) is reused
    verbatim as the pinned Dart/AOT runtime for this derivative; the pin is
    recorded in tools/fetch-flutter-engine-prebuilt.sh.

  Per-release details are recorded in CHANGELOG.md. Historical entries in
  CHANGELOG.md describe upstream Rodin Essential releases and are retained
  in their original wording.


